{# BJJ Systems Template V3 - Jinja2 #}
{# Generates markdown from TEMPLATE.json for system/methodology content #}
{# A/B Testing: variant-a-show/variant-b-hide CSS classes #}

---
title: "{{name}} | BJJ System | BJJ Graph"
description: "{{description}}"
---

{# PostHog A/B Testing Metadata #}
<body data-content-type="systems">

<!-- Schema Markup - Auto-generated from JSON -->
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "HowTo",
  "name": "How to Implement {{name}}",
  "description": "Step-by-step implementation sequence for {{name}}.",
  "step": [
    {%- for step in implementation_sequence[:8] %}
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "name": "{{step.phase}}",
      "text": "{{step.description}}",
      "position": {{loop.index}}
    }{{ "," if not loop.last else "" }}
    {%- endfor %}
  ]
}
</script>

<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "WebPage",
  "name": "{{name}}",
  "description": "{{description}}",
  "url": "https://bjjgraph.org/Systems/{{name.replace(' ', '-')}}",
  "isPartOf": {
    "@type": "WebSite",
    "name": "BJJ Graph",
    "url": "https://bjjgraph.org"
  }
}
</script>

<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
  "itemListElement": [
    {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://bjjgraph.org/"},
    {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Systems", "item": "https://bjjgraph.org/Systems/"},
    {"@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "{{name}}", "item": "https://bjjgraph.org/Systems/{{name.replace(' ', '-')}}"}
  ]
}
</script>

<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {%- for obstacle in common_obstacles[:6] %}
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": "What is a common obstacle: {{obstacle.obstacle}}?",
      "acceptedAnswer": {
        "@type": "Answer",
        "text": "{{obstacle.solution}}"
      }
    }{{ "," if not loop.last else "" }}
    {%- endfor %}
  ]
}
</script>

{% if summary %}
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "DefinedTerm",
  "name": "{{name}}",
  "description": "{{summary}}",
  "inDefinedTermSet": "https://bjjgraph.org/Systems/"
}
</script>
{% endif %}

{# Metadata chips — single scannable row (replaces the old filler blockquote + duplicate bold lines) #}
<div class="principle-meta">
<span class="meta-chip">{{system_type}}</span>
<span class="meta-chip">{{difficulty_level}} difficulty</span>
</div>

{# Flexbox wrapper for A/B testing #}
<main class="content-wrapper" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column;">

<section id="overview" class="content-section">

{% set is_plural = name.endswith('s') and not name.endswith('ss') -%}
## What {{ 'are' if is_plural else 'is' }} {{name}}?

{% if summary %}**{{summary}}**

{% endif -%}
{{overview}}

</section>

{% set member_count = (related_content | rejectattr('content_type', 'equalto', 'System') | list | length) %}
{# Only a product whose affiliate_url was OPENED and confirmed to resolve to that exact
   instructional may render (content/Systems/*.json → link_status: "live", link_checked: date).
   A missing or non-"live" status renders NOTHING and falls through to the free study section
   below: a 404 or a guessed link earns nothing and costs trust, so an empty slot is the honest
   default. Fail-safe by construction — a new product without a verification date cannot ship a
   CTA. See docs/Affiliate.md. #}
{% set live_products = (products or []) | selectattr('link_status', 'defined') | selectattr('link_status', 'equalto', 'live') | list %}
{% if live_products %}
<section id="unlock-this-system" class="content-section product-cards">

## Unlock This System

<p class="section-subtitle">Go deeper with the instructional that built this system.</p>

<!-- PROXIMATE AFFILIATE DISCLOSURE — required HERE, not only in terms.md. FTC 16 CFR Part 255
     and the UK ASA/CAP code both require it clear, conspicuous and close to the link. Placed
     above the cards so a reader who scans only the card still sees it. CANONICAL WORDING lives
     in docs/Affiliate.md; the app CTA in neural/src/app.src.jsx carries the same sentence, and
     scripts/check_affiliate_surface.py fails the build if the copies drift or if a sponsored
     link ever renders without its disclosure above it. -->
<p class="affiliate-disclosure">BJJGraph earns a commission if you buy through this link, at no extra cost to you. It never changes what the graph teaches.</p>

<div class="product-cards-grid">
{% for p in live_products %}
<article class="product-card" data-product-id="{{ p.id | default('') }}">
<div class="product-card__holo" aria-hidden="true"></div>
<div class="product-card__shine" aria-hidden="true"></div>
{% if p.image %}<div class="product-card__cover"><img src="{{ p.image }}" alt="{{ p.title }}" loading="lazy" width="640" height="360" /><span class="product-card__vendor-badge">{{ p.vendor | default('BJJFanatics') }}</span></div>{% endif %}
<div class="product-card__body">
<h3 class="product-card__title">{{ p.title }}</h3>
{% if p.instructor %}<p class="product-card__instructor">with {{ p.instructor }}</p>{% endif %}
<span class="product-card__unlocks-badge">Unlocks {{ member_count }} technique{{ 's' if member_count != 1 else '' }} in this system</span>
{% if p.blurb %}<p class="product-card__blurb">{{ p.blurb }}</p>{% endif %}
</div>
<a class="product-card__cta affiliate-link" href="{{ p.affiliate_url | with_utm(name, p.id | default('')) }}" target="_blank" rel="sponsored nofollow noopener" data-affiliate="true" data-product-id="{{ p.id | default('') }}" data-system-slug="systems/{{ name | slugify }}" data-system-name="{{ name }}" data-vendor="{{ (p.vendor | default('bjjfanatics')) | lower }}" data-position="{{ loop.index0 }}">{# NO PRICE IN THE LABEL. price_usd is authored reference data we cannot keep fresh — every
   value on file was wrong (by up to 3.6x) when checked against the vendor on 2026-08-09, and
   "Get it · $97" landing on a $349 checkout is the same broken promise as a dead link. The
   vendor's own page is the only truthful price surface. #}Get the instructional <span class="product-card__cta-arrow" aria-hidden="true">&#8594;</span></a>
</article>
{% endfor %}
</div>

</section>
{% else %}
{# NO VERIFIED PRODUCT — the common case (44 of 47 systems). The page must still look finished
   and still teach, so the slot the product cards would have filled carries the FREE next step
   instead of an empty region. Deliberately no outbound vendor link: a generic shop URL nobody
   verified would be exactly the guess this pipeline forbids. #}
<section id="study-this-system" class="content-section system-study-free">

## How do you drill {{name}}?

<p class="section-subtitle">There's no instructional attached to this system yet &mdash; and you don't need one. It's taught here, free, from the {{member_count}} technique{{ 's' if member_count != 1 else '' }} it strings together.</p>

- **Learn it in order** &mdash; the [implementation sequence](#implementation-sequence) is the path, not a list.
- **Study each piece** &mdash; every technique in [this system's map](#related-content) has its own page, flashcards and film study.
- **Then roll it** &mdash; on the [interactive graph](/) these same nodes light up as your game moves through them.

</section>
{% endif %}

<section id="unlock-graph" class="content-section system-unlock" data-system-unlock hidden>

## Unlock this part of the graph

<p class="section-subtitle">This system teaches the highlighted nodes in the graph. Mark what you already know &mdash; be honest, it's your game.</p>

<div class="system-progress" data-system-progress>
<svg class="system-progress__ring" viewBox="0 0 44 44" aria-hidden="true"><circle class="system-progress__ring-bg" cx="22" cy="22" r="19"></circle><circle class="system-progress__ring-fill" cx="22" cy="22" r="19"></circle></svg>
<div class="system-progress__text">You've unlocked <strong class="system-progress__known">0</strong> / <span class="system-progress__total">0</span> techniques in this system</div>
<button class="system-progress__mark-all" data-mark-system type="button">Mark whole system as known</button>
</div>

<ul class="system-members" data-system-members></ul>

</section>

<section id="key-principles" class="content-section">

## Core Principles
{% for principle in key_principles -%}
- {{principle}}
{% endfor %}

</section>

<section id="key-components" class="content-section">

## Key Components
{% for component in key_components -%}
**{{component.component_name}}** ({{component.purpose}})
{{component.description}}

{% endfor %}

</section>

<section id="implementation-sequence" class="content-section">

## Implementation Sequence
{% for step in implementation_sequence -%}
{{step.step_number}}. **{{step.phase}}**: {{step.description}}
{% if step.key_points -%}
Key points:
{% for point in step.key_points -%}
  - {{point}}
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

{% endfor %}

</section>

<section id="common-obstacles" class="content-section hide-minimal">

## What Challenges Will You Face?
{% for obstacle in common_obstacles -%}
- **{{obstacle.obstacle}}**: {{obstacle.solution}}
{% endfor %}

</section>

<section id="assessment-metrics" class="content-section">

## How to Measure Your Progress
{% for metric in assessment_metrics -%}
**{{metric.metric_name}}**: {{metric.description}}
Proficiency indicators:
{% for indicator in metric.proficiency_indicators -%}
- {{indicator}}
{% endfor %}

{% endfor %}

</section>

<section id="training-methodology" class="content-section hide-minimal">

## How to Train This System Effectively

### Drilling Approach
{{training_methodology.drilling_approach}}

### Progression Path
{% for stage in training_methodology.progression_path -%}
**{{stage.stage}}** (Focus: {{stage.focus}}){% if stage.timeframe %} - {{stage.timeframe}}{% endif %}
{% endfor %}

### Common Mistakes
{% for mistake in training_methodology.common_mistakes -%}
- {{mistake}}
{% endfor %}

</section>

<section id="related-content" class="content-section">

## Which Positions, Transitions, and Principles Connect to This System?

{% for item in related_content -%}
- [[{{item.name}}]] ({{item.content_type}}) - {{item.relationship}}
{% endfor %}

</section>

</main>
